  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Set at the Nouveau Port in Cavalaire, La Suite serves world cuisine with Italian influences, in an air-conditioned setting extended by a large terrace with harbour views.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go — dog policy unresolved</h2>
      <p>⚠️ Despite a dedicated search, no reliable source confirms whether this restaurant accepts dogs: neither the Cavalaire-sur-Mer tourist office, nor the restaurant's website, nor any customer review mentions it for "La Suite" (not to be confused with "Le Bateau Ivre", another restaurant at the Nouveau Port that officially confirms it accepts pets). Better to call before going with your dog than to rely on unverified information. Budget around €21-30 for the meal. The air-conditioned dining room is a real plus on hot days, and the available wifi lets you extend your stay if needed.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: contrary to what this listing said before, dog access here is not confirmed by any reliable source — call before you come, or try Le Bateau Ivre instead, a little further along the same harbour, which officially confirms it accepts pets.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cavalaire harbour and its promenade are right nearby, perfect for a digestive walk with your dog before or after the meal.</p>
